*
* START-DESCRIPTION:
*
* CALL !KEEPSELECT
*
* Sets the KEEP.SELECT flag of the command now running.  With OPTION CLEAR.SELECT the command processor clears list 0 at
* the end of a command that found the list active (CPROC); a program that means to leave what is left of it says so with
* KEEP.SELECT and the list stays.  Without CLEAR.SELECT the statement does nothing, as the manual says.  The flag is
* cleared as each outermost command starts.
*
* END-DESCRIPTION
*
* START-CODE

$internal
subroutine keepsel
$catalog !keepselect

$include int$keys.h

   void kernel(K$KEEP.SELECT, 1)
   return
end

* END-CODE
